+ 2.\\n\\nIn 1900 Fej´er [15] established that the trigonometric polynomial\\n\\n1+2\\n\\nN\\n\\nX\\n\\nj=1 1−j\\n\\nN+ 1cos jt\\n\\nis nonnegative by proving for it the representation\\n\\n1+2\\n\\nN\\n\\nX\\n\\nj=1 1−j\\n\\nN+ 1cos jt =1\\n\\nN+ 1 Φ(2)\\n\\nN(t),\\n\\nwhere\\n\\nΦ(2)\\n\\nN(t) = sin N+1\\n\\n2 t\\n\\nsin t\\n\\n2!2\\n\\n.\\n\\nFurther, Fej´er [23, 16] established an extremal property of Φ(2)\\n\\nN(t): the\\n\\nmaximum of a nonnegative trigonometric polynomial 1+P N\\n\\nj=1 a j cos jt\\n\\ndoes not exceed N+ 1, with equality attained solely for 1\\n\\nN+1 Φ(2)\\n\\nN(t) and\\n\\nonly at the points 2 πk,k= 0,±1,±2,....\\n\\nThe functions Φ(1)\\n\\nN(t) and Φ(2)\\n\\nN(t) are called Fej´er kernels and have\\n\\nvarious extremal properties [6, 11].\\n\\n24 DMITRIY DMITRISHIN, ANDREY SMORODIN, AND ALEX STOKOLOS\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nIndo-Slovenia Pre-Conference School on (https://events.iitbhilai.ac.in/caldam2024/pre-conf/yrfAbstract.pdf)\\nciteturn2search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.8 years ago; Alcon et al. [1] proposed the following conjecture for Mycielski graph ... constructions for neighbor-locating colorings of graphs. ... Mojdeh, D.A.: On the conjectures of neighbor locating coloring of graphs.\\nLocating and neighbor-locating colorings of\\ngraphs\\nSupraja D K\\nIndian Institute of Technology Dharwad, India\\ndksupraja95@gmail.com\\nAbstract. A proper k-vertex-coloring of a graph G is a neighbor-locating\\nk-coloring if for each pair of vertices in the same color class, the sets of\\ncolors found in their neighborhoods are different. The neighbor-locating\\nchromatic number χNL(G) is the minimum k for which G admits a\\nneighbor-locating k-coloring. A proper k-vertex-coloring of a graph G\\nis a locating k-coloring if for each pair of vertices x and y in the same\\ncolor-class, there exists a color class Si such that d(x, Si) ̸= d(y, Si). The\\nlocating chromatic number χL(G) is the minimum k for which G admits\\na locating k-coloring. It follows that χ(G) ≤χL(G) ≤χNL(G) for any\\ngraph G, where χ(G) is the usual chromatic number of G.\\nIt is shown that for any three integers p, q, r with 2 ≤p ≤q ≤r (ex-\\ncept when 2 = p = q < r), there exists a connected graph Gp,q,r with\\nχ(Gp,q,r) = p, χL(Gp,q,r) = q and χNL(Gp,q,r) = r [2]. It is interest-\\ning to know under what conditions does a graph have neighbor-locating\\nnumber equal to locating chromatic number (resp. chromatic number).\\nAlcon et al. [1] proposed the following conjecture for Mycielski graph\\nµ(G) of a graph G: For every graph G, χNL(µ(G)) = χNL(G) + 1.\\nTill date, the conjecture is proved for complete multipartite graphs [1],\\npaths, cycles, fans, wheels and comb graphs [3]. The conjecture still re-\\nmains open.\\nReferences\\n1. Alcon, L., Gutierrez, M., Hernando, C., Mora, M., Pelayo, I.M.: Neighbor-locating\\ncolorings in graphs. Theoretical Computer Science 806, 144–155 (2020)\\n2. Chakraborty, D., Foucaud, F., Nandi, S., Sen, S., Supraja, D.K.: New bounds and\\nconstructions for neighbor-locating colorings of graphs. In: Algorithms and Discrete\\nApplied Mathematics: 9th International Conference, CALDAM 2023, Gandhinagar,\\nIndia, February 9–11, 2023, Proceedings. pp. 121–133. Springer (2023)\\n3. Mojdeh, D.A.: On the conjectures of neighbor locating coloring of graphs. Theoret-\\nical Computer Science 922, 300–307 (2022)\\n13--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nNeighbor Locating Coloring on Graphs: Three Products — 89 (https://combinatorialpress.com/article/jcmcc/Volume%20122/neighbor-locating-coloring-on-graphs-three-products.pdf)\\nciteturn2search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; *Electronic Journal of Graph Theory and Applications, 12*(1), pp.55-73. ... Neighbor-locating colorings in graphs. ... On the conjectures of neighbor-locating coloring of graphs.\\nNeighbor Locating Coloring on Gra